   "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_pipit",
   "description": "Species of bird",
   "extract": "The tree pipit is a small passerine bird that breeds throughout most of Europe and the Palearctic as far east as the East Siberian Mountains. It is a long-distance migrant, migrating in winter to Africa and southern Asia. The scientific name is from Latin: anthus is the name of a small bird of grasslands, and the specific  trivialis means \"common\".",
